These instructions are for Windows
To set up a virtual environment 
type the following in the terminal in VSCode (where you have the GitHub repository)

python -m venv .venv

The activate it by typing the following into your terminal 

python -m venv .venv

If successful, you should have (.venv) in green in front of each line in the terminal.

Then you need to pull the requirements.txt file and install it into the virtual environment by typing

pip install -r requirements.txt

This should install all the packages into your virtual environment.

If you install other packages you need to update the requirements.txt file. To do this type

pip freeze > requirements.txt

Then push that file onto GitHub and tell us that it has been updated so that we can install the new packages
